'''Banda''' is an [[Austronesian languages|Austronesian]] language of the [[Central Maluku languages|Central Maluku subgroup]]. Along with [[Kei language|Kei]], it is one of the two languages of the [[Kei Islands]] in the [[Indonesia]]n province of [[Maluku (province)|Maluku]].

Originally, the Banda language was spoken on the [[Banda Islands]] until the [[Dutch conquest of the Banda Islands|Dutch military campaign]] in 1621, during which almost all indigenous inhabitants were killed, enslaved or exiled. Survivors of the campaign found refuge on the island of [[Kai Besar|Kei Besar]], where the language is still in active use in the villages ''Banda Elat'' and ''Banda Eli''.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Collins |first1=James T. |last2=Kaartinen |first2=Timo |year=1998 |title=Preliminary Notes on Bandanese Language Maintenance and Change in Kei |journal=Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde |volume=154 |issue=4 |pages=521–570 |doi=10.1163/22134379-90003884 |jstor=27865462|doi-access=free }}</ref>

